      <activity id="e3d40569-5d7c-5c5d-ad6f-9d4b00ec480d" activityNameId="f7204db9-52e2-5876-8e49-73326847f561" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="2" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Window frame, wood, opaquely painted, U=1.0 W/m2K, Baumgartner, wall opening, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Window frame, wood, opaquely painted, U=1.0 W/m2K, Baumgartner, wall opening, at plant
The measures of the window are 1.75m (width) x 1.3m (height). The wall opening is 1.8 m2 (assumption width of frame 0.12m, 2/3 of frame are behind the wall opening). The bill of materials is based on data from Baumgartner Fenster.;
UUID: 74915c71-54fa-3aa1-b27b-c6d86c00acea
Included are the materials used in a wooden window frame (with surface treatment). Production losses, work materials, packaging materials, energy demand and the transport of the materials are also included.
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: Saphir integral 67/55; Industry data.
Time period: Time of publications
Production volume: na
Sampling: Data survey at window manufacturer Baumgartner in Switzerland. 
Extrapolations: Some generic datasets from ecoinvent have been used.
Uncertainty adjustments: None
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_74915c71-54fa-3aa1-b27b-c6d86c00acea.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
